        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm trying to recall where the root वस appears in the Dhatupatha — it seems to be listed in curadi (class 10) with the sense निवासे, though I'm second-guessing whether it's actually grouped under \"वस स्नेहच्छेदापहरणेषु\" instead.\n\nIf it's adanta (ending in अ with lopa, no vṛddhi), the future would be वसयिष्यन्ति; otherwise it would be वासयिष्यन्ति, so I'm trying to pin down which list it belongs to in the Siddhanta Kaumudi's adanta section by recalling the sequence of roots like कथ, वर, गण, शठ, पट, रह, स्तन, पत, पष.\n\nContinuing through that enumeration, I'm recalling further adanta roots — स्वर, रच, कल, चह, मह, सार, स्पृह, भाम, सूच, खेट, खोट, गोम, कुमार, शील, साम, वेल, पल्यूल, वात — trying to locate वस निवासे somewhere in this traditional list to confirm its classification.\n\nI'm trying to recall whether \"वस\" without the nasal mark signals an adanta root in this dhatupatha convention, similar to how \"कथ\" is written for non-adanta curadi roots — I'm still not fully certain which classification applies here.\n\nSince the format seems to indicate anubandha markers are preserved, the absence of ँ suggests \"वस\" is adanta, meaning the future form should be वसयिष्यन्ति rather than the snehachheda sense form. I'll go with वसयिष्यन्ति as my answer.\n\n",
        "signature": ""
      },
